%% Tutoring chat (StudyChat.tsx). Corrected: no Lovable AI Gateway fallback exists in
%% frontend/src/routes/api/chat.ts today; that path has been removed from this diagram.
sequenceDiagram
  actor Student
  participant UI as StudyChat.tsx
  participant I18n as I18nProvider + detectLanguage (lib/i18n/detect.ts)
  participant Fn as Authenticated server functions
  participant Cloud as external Supabase threads/messages
  participant API as frontend/src/routes/api/chat.ts POST /api/chat
  participant PY as Local Python backend FastAPI /api/chat
  participant RAG as Context Manager + retrieval
  participant LLM as Local Qwen via llama.cpp
  Student->>UI: Open /chat
  UI->>Fn: listThreads or createThread
  Fn->>Cloud: User-scoped thread operation
  Cloud-->>Fn: Thread
  UI-->>Student: Navigate /chat/{threadId}
  UI->>Fn: listMessages(threadId)
  Fn->>Cloud: User-scoped ordered messages
  Cloud-->>UI: Persisted UI messages
  Student->>UI: Submit question
  UI->>I18n: detectLanguage(text) + effectiveResponseLanguage(text, uiLanguage)
  I18n-->>UI: responseLanguageHint, CLIENT STATE ONLY, kept per message
  UI-->>Student: Optimistic message + Thinking indicator
  UI->>API: UI messages + threadId + academicYear + gradeLevel, bearer token<br/>responseLanguageHint is NOT included in this payload today
  API->>Cloud: Verify thread ownership (threads.id + user_id), then insert user message
  API->>PY: requestContextAnswer (context-backend.server.ts): question + subject/language/year/grade, stream:false
  PY->>RAG: Build budgeted context and provenance
  RAG-->>PY: Relevant chunks and memory
  PY->>LLM: Compiled context + current question
  LLM-->>PY: Answer text (response-language enforcement NOT implemented today)
  PY-->>API: ContextChatResponse: answer, sources, used_model, retrieval_summary
  API->>Cloud: Insert completed assistant message (onFinish)
  API-->>UI: AI SDK stream: text-start/text-delta/text-end + data part context-metadata
  UI-->>Student: Markdown answer + exam tip + collapsible sources
  opt Listen / Stop read-aloud
    Student->>UI: Click Listen on a completed assistant message
    UI->>UI: speechLocaleFor(answerText, uiLanguage), lib/speech.ts<br/>Web Speech API, ephemeral, never stored
    UI-->>Student: Spoken answer, or graceful no-op when unsupported/no voice
  end
  opt Python backend unreachable or returns an error
    API-->>UI: HTTP error with ContextBackendError.status (default 503) and message
    UI-->>Student: Error surfaced in chat. No fallback answer is generated
  end
  Note over PY,LLM: FUTURE CODEX IMPLEMENTATION: ui_language, message_language and effective<br/>response_language contract. message_language should win only when confidently<br/>one of the seven approved languages (en/de/gsw/ru/es/fr/it).
